    "summary": "The Somali National Army has launched a training program for local youth in Waajid, Bakool region, aimed at boosting security ahead of a planned handover of security responsibilities.",
    "content": "The Somali National Army (SNA) has commenced a training program for local youth in Waajid district, located in the Bakool region of southwestern Somalia. The initiative, which began this week, is designed to prepare recruits to maintain security in Waajid and its surrounding areas.\n\nAccording to military officials, the training is part of a broader strategy to enhance the capacity of Somali security forces stationed in the district. The recruits are expected to collaborate with the SNA and the South West State's Darawish forces. Their duties will include guarding key installations, preventing attacks, and supporting security operations in and around Waajid.\n\nThe program comes as Somalia prepares for the eventual transition of security responsibilities from the African Union Transition Mission in Somalia (ATMIS) to Somali forces. The handover, scheduled to be completed by the end of 2026, has prompted increased efforts to recruit and train local personnel across various regions.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development signals a continued push toward self-reliance in security matters. Many diaspora members have family ties to the Bakool region and closely follow efforts to stabilize areas that have historically faced threats from insurgent groups. The involvement of local youth in security forces is often seen as a positive step toward creating jobs and fostering community-based protection.\n\nWhile the training program is a localized effort, it reflects the broader national objective of building a capable and professional army. The success of such initiatives will be critical in ensuring a smooth transition and long-term stability. The international community, including Somalia's partners, has emphasized the importance of supporting these grassroots security measures.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/15/ciidamo-deegaan-oo-waajid-lagu-tababarayo-ka-hor-wareejinta-masuuliyadda-amniga/",
