    "summary": "The National Electoral Commission states that the Towfiiq Party was barred from Galmudug's indirect elections due to procedural non-compliance, not political motives.",
    "content": "The National Electoral Commission (NEC) of Somalia has provided an explanation for the exclusion of the Towfiiq Party, led by Sheikh Shakir, from the ongoing indirect elections in the Galmudug regional state. According to NEC spokesman Abdifatah Faysal Hussein, the decision was based on the party's failure to meet the necessary procedural requirements, and was not politically motivated.\n\nHussein stated that the Towfiiq Party did not submit an official application to the NEC expressing its intent to participate in the electoral process. This lack of formal submission meant the party did not fulfill the criteria set for political organizations seeking to take part.\n\nThe NEC's announcement comes amid heightened political activity in Galmudug as the region conducts its indirect elections. The commission has emphasized the importance of adhering to established regulations to ensure a transparent and orderly process.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the exclusion of a party from the electoral process underscores the importance of adhering to official procedures, which many in the diaspora follow closely as they support democratic development in their homeland. The diaspora has historically played a significant role in Somali politics, both through remittances and direct engagement.\n\nThe NEC's clarification aims to address any concerns about the fairness of the electoral process in Galmudug. It reiterates that all political entities must comply with the same rules to participate.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/14/guddiga-doorashooyinka-qaranka-oo-ka-hadlay-ka-reebista-ururka-towfiiq-doorashada-ku-celiska-ah-ee-galmudug/",
